1
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:25,620
You catch anything?

2
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:33,781
Sorry, I didn't mean to
sneak up on you like that.

3
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:41,600
My name's Nishida, and I'm a fisherman.

4
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:43,620
In the game, anyway.

5
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:45,017
Back in Japan,

6
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:49,577
I was the head of network security for a
company called Toto High Speed Internet.

7
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:50,680
I'm Kirito.

8
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:54,540
Wait, wasn't Toto the company that... Yep.

9
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:58,527
We were the folks in charge of
network security for this game.

10
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:04,600
It's a big one!

11
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:07,240
Yeah, but I've cut bigger.

12
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:10,550
Whoa!

13
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:14,120
Awesome. Thanks.

14
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,097
I'm good at catching
them, but cooking them?

15
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:18,260
Yeah, not so good.

16
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:21,677
I'd love to make sashimi
or a nice stew out of them,

17
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:24,878
But what's the point when
I don't have any soy sauce?

18
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:29,937
I could go for fish baked with soy sauce
right now, or with radishes with soy sauce.

19
00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:33,837
Hey, if you want, I just might be
able to help you out with that.

20
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:35,260
Wait, say what?

21
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:23,460
I'll fill up all my dreams.

22
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:27,000
I can't sleep with my head.

23
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:28,919
What is your body?

24
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:33,880
How many heart can you reach me?

25
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,100
I'm going to spread out.

26
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:41,597
How do you feel?

27
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:43,327
The body of my body is weak,

28
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:59,077
I wanna always be waiting!

29
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:02,100
I'll give you everything I have!

30
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:16,037
That was an amazing meal!

31
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:19,360
I had no idea you could get
soy sauce in this world!

32
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:21,557
Actually, I made it myself!

33
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:23,857
If you want, you can
take some home with you.

34
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:24,770
Really?

35
00:03:25,060 --> 00:03:28,140
Man, my taste buds bow down before you.

36
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:30,317
Glad you liked it!

37
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:32,929
By the way, how high
is your fishing skill?

38
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:36,984
I'm asking because Kirito hasn't
been able to catch anything yet.

39
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:42,344
Yeah, well, maybe if all the lakes
on this floor weren't so hard!

40
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:44,900
Well, actually, that's not true.

41
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,840
As far as fishing goes,

42
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:51,437
the only lake that's tough to catch anything
in is the big one you were at today.

43
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:52,350
What?

44
00:03:52,433 --> 00:03:54,160
Why would someone design it like that?

45
00:03:54,460 --> 00:03:55,880
Yes, good question!

46
00:03:56,540 --> 00:03:58,977
That lake is the home of...

47
00:03:59,060 --> 00:04:02,060
the king of all fish. Seriously?

48
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:04,940
Yep, we're old pals.

49
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:07,697
I've had him on the end of
my hook quite a few times.

50
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:12,180
But he's so strong, he yanks the pole
right out of my hands every time.

51
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:18,400
I was wondering, do you
have any plans for tomorrow?

52
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:26,937
I don't mind helping the old guy out.

53
00:04:27,020 --> 00:04:30,457
But how am I supposed to do a
switch move with a fishing pole?

54
00:04:30,540 --> 00:04:33,422
You're the only one I know
who can figure it out.

55
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:38,797
What if you catch it?

56
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:39,880
Will you keep it?

57
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:41,420
Is that even possible?

58
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:50,149
He is pretty cool,
though, don't you think?

59
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:53,734
When you both showed up, I
was like, who is this person?

60
00:04:56,440 --> 00:05:00,240
Isn't it funny how people are
living normal lives in this world?

61
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:04,157
And since we're the
ones on the front lines,

62
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:06,697
their lives have sort of
become our responsibility,

63
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:07,610
haven't they?

64
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:12,800
For me, I wasn't getting
stronger for anyone else.

65
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:15,280
It was just about me staying alive.

66
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:22,809
Everyone expects great
things from you now.

67
00:05:22,940 --> 00:05:24,640
And guess what? So do I.

68
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:27,151
Talk about pressure, huh?

69
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:32,660
Yeah, I promised I'd save everyone.

70
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:35,245
Hell of a thing to live up to.

71
00:05:38,620 --> 00:05:39,477
Oh, well.

72
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:42,089
They'll understand if
you take tonight off.

73
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:43,350
Yeah.

74
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:53,840
Oh, my God.

75
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:57,167
Can you believe all the
people who showed up?

76
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,000
Well, here we go.

77
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:03,417
Thanks for your patience, everyone.

78
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:06,197
Here comes today's main
event. It's about time.

79
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:09,520
Kirito, let's catch us a fish. Yeah.

80
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:15,368
How big is this thing
supposed to be anyway?

81
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:18,240
Okay, here goes nothing!

82
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:44,920
Um, shouldn't you reel it in? No, not yet!

83
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:48,220
Uh, Nishida?

84
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:50,200
Hang on, not yet.

85
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:53,390
Now!

86
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:55,140
I got this sucker!

87
00:06:58,160 --> 00:06:59,300
Uh, switch?

88
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:06,580
Come here, you bastard!

89
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:10,750
Look!

90
00:07:10,833 --> 00:07:11,663
It's coming up!

91
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:20,700
I think I tired him out.

92
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:25,120
Where are you going? Hey!

93
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:31,000
No, no, no, no!

94
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:34,160
Cait! Look out!

95
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:37,260
For what?

96
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:52,500
You ran away!

97
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:54,171
You left me there to die!

98
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:55,960
Here it comes!

99
00:07:57,760 --> 00:07:59,100
Whoa, we can run?

100
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:02,040
It's like a crazy lungfish.

101
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:04,000
Kirito, this is serious.

102
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:05,677
That thing's coming for us.

103
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:06,936
Hurry, do something.

104
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:08,680
Yeah, I'm still thinking.

105
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:11,226
Guess I'll take care of this.

106
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:16,180
Run while you still can.

107
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:17,640
Nah, she'll be fine.

108
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:21,000
Save your wife, Kirito.

109
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:23,940
No, watch out!

110
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,360
Oh, wow.

111
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:39,620
That was badass!

112
00:08:40,340 --> 00:08:41,600
You're Asuna, right?

113
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:43,277
What are you doing here?

114
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:44,478
Man, this is Asuna.

115
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:47,260
Can I shake your hand?

116
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,340
Nice job, honey.

117
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:54,630
Heathcliff.

118
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:07,377
come on you've moped long
enough already I know but it's

119
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:10,737
only been two weeks if he needs
us on the front lines then

120
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:13,077
something must have happened
why else would he interrupt

121
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:18,460
our vacation yeah but still
let's at least hear what he's

122
00:09:25,780 --> 00:09:26,610
got to say.

123
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:27,817
Come on, time to go.

124
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:30,217
We'll take care of this, then come back.

125
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:31,220
You got it.

126
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:36,151
Thanks for seeing us off.

127
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:40,264
I know we didn't get to spend much
time together, but it was fun.

128
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:44,177
Oh, well, it was an honor and a privilege.

129
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:46,077
Actually, before I met the two of you,

130
00:09:46,160 --> 00:09:49,897
I couldn't imagine what the folks
working to clear the game were like.

131
00:09:49,980 --> 00:09:52,804
You might as well have
been from another planet.

132
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:56,167
Being trapped in here
for the past two years,

133
00:09:57,300 --> 00:10:01,660
even if I made it out alive, I don't
know if I can go back to my old job,

134
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:02,980
my old life.

135
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:07,280
Maybe deep down inside, I've
given up hope of ever getting out.

136
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:09,637
I figured spending my
time with the fishing

137
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:12,700
pole between my mitts was
the best thing for me.

138
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:14,240
Pretty sad, huh?

139
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:15,670
Uh-uh.

140
00:10:15,753 --> 00:10:16,800
That isn't sad.

141
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:18,396
I get what you mean.

142
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:22,464
I used to feel the same
as you, at first anyway.

143
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,680
I felt lost and hopeless.

144
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:27,500
Every night I'd cry myself to sleep.

145
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:32,784
It felt like each day that went by in here
was another day lost from my real life.

146
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:35,520
So, I'd cry.

147
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:38,760
And afterwards I'd go and
fight as hard as I could.

148
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:43,357
All I cared about was winning, getting
stronger, and getting to the next floor.

149
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:48,160
But then, I was walking along and I
saw someone taking a nap in the shade.

150
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:50,200
I was so mad.

151
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:53,482
I told him he shouldn't
waste his time like that.

152
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:55,500
And then he said,

153
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:57,077
and I'll never forget it,

154
00:10:57,160 --> 00:11:00,757
this is Aincrad's best season and today's
weather is at its optimal setting.

155
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:05,075
He said it'd be a waste to go into
some dungeon on such a beautiful day.

156
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:07,997
So I tried lying down
too, and you know what?

157
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:09,340
I slept like a baby.

158
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:14,578
When I woke up, it was evening and
he was giving me the weirdest look.

159
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:17,417
Anyway, we formed our own party.

160
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:19,676
And that's when I realized something.

161
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:24,440
Even in a world like this,
he was really living.

162
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:27,417
He wasn't losing a day in the real world.

163
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,097
He was gaining a day.

164
00:11:29,180 --> 00:11:30,200
Here.

165
00:11:31,220 --> 00:11:32,997
I learned so much from him.

166
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:35,360
And by him, I mean Kirito.

167
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:38,697
When I thought about him
before falling asleep?

168
00:11:38,780 --> 00:11:40,956
I noticed I wouldn't have nightmares.

169
00:11:41,420 --> 00:11:44,040
I began looking forward
to seeing him again.

170
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:49,360
It was like, for the first
time, I was glad I was here.

171
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,647
Kijito was everything to me.

172
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:56,273
He's what the last two years were about.

173
00:11:56,860 --> 00:11:58,360
He's proof I'm alive.

174
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:02,714
Why'd I put on the nerve gear that day?

175
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:06,300
It's obvious, so I could
come here and meet him.

176
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:08,937
You're still alive, right?

177
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:11,597
You must have something to live for, too.

178
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:13,957
Yeah, you're right.

179
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:16,397
Yeah, you're absolutely right.

180
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:18,997
Life isn't so bad here.

181
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:22,060
No, it's actually pretty damn good.

182
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:28,337
I wish there was something I could
do to help, but well, there it is.

183
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:30,037
Good luck and be safe.

184
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:32,677
Don't worry, we'll go fishing again.

185
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:34,520
Take care. Okay.

186
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:40,180
Teleport, Gransom!

187
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:56,180
The recon team was wiped out?

188
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:58,917
They were scouting for
the upcoming boss fight.

189
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:02,706
It was a party of 20 members,
taken from five different guilds.

190
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:05,851
Ten of them reached the center of the room

191
00:13:05,940 --> 00:13:07,280
Then the boss appeared

192
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:12,447
And that's when the entrance closed
Cutting them off from the rest of the party

193
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,420
They walked into an anti-crystal zone

194
00:13:17,140 --> 00:13:18,857
Precisely And it couldn't
have been more than

195
00:13:18,940 --> 00:13:21,705
five minutes or so When
the door finally opened

196
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:25,717
The room was empty There wasn't any trace

197
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:28,857
left behind of the ten
soldiers Or the boss

198
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:31,917
You're kidding Now more
than ever Clearing the

199
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:34,557
game should be everyone's
number one priority.

200
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:37,837
We're going to launch an attack with
the largest group we can assemble.

201
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:42,340
You can count on us to fight with
you, but this needs to be clear.

202
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:44,524
Austin's safety is my priority.

203
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:48,437
If things start to get hairy in
there, I'm going to protect her.

204
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:49,814
That's not negotiable.

205
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:53,849
A person with something to
protect is a strong ally to have.

206
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:56,478
I'm expecting a good fight from you.

207
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:05,085
Three more hours of
waiting, what should we do?

208
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:10,254
What's wrong with you?

209
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:16,871
There's something I have to ask you,
but I don't want you getting mad at me.

210
00:14:17,620 --> 00:14:21,440
Instead of going to the boss
fight, could you please stay here?

211
00:14:22,680 --> 00:14:24,140
Why would you ask that?

212
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:29,682
We won't be able to use teleport crystals,
so there's no telling what could happen.

213
00:14:30,460 --> 00:14:31,420
I'm scared.

214
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:33,737
If anything happened to you, I...

215
00:14:33,820 --> 00:14:35,957
So you want to go to someplace dangerous,

216
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:39,840
alone, and you expect me to
stay here, where it's safe?

217
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:46,197
You know what would happen
if you didn't come back?

218
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:47,110
Huh?

219
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:49,720
I'd kill myself.

220
00:14:50,940 --> 00:14:55,764
I'd never forgive myself for staying behind,
so what would be the point in living?

221
00:14:57,240 --> 00:15:02,780
I'm sorry I guess I'm losing my nerve
all I want to do is run away with you

222
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:05,517
I don't care if we never
make it back to the

223
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:08,537
real world I just want to live with you In

224
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:12,617
our little house in the
woods it'd be nice if

225
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:16,360
we could do that be
together every day forever

226
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:20,897
Have you ever thought
about what's happening

227
00:15:20,980 --> 00:15:23,397
in the real world about
what's happening to

228
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:28,137
our Bodies while we're in here a few weeks

229
00:15:28,220 --> 00:15:30,157
after the game was launched
do you Remember what

230
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:32,677
happened most of the players suddenly went

231
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:36,717
offline and Stayed that
way for a few hours my

232
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:38,857
guess is that's when
all the players bodies

233
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:41,705
Were being moved to
hospitals in the real world

234
00:15:42,660 --> 00:15:47,257
That's where we all are right now in
hospitals barely being kept alive by

235
00:15:47,340 --> 00:15:52,797
Machines it's hard to believe we're gonna
survive like that for much longer so?

236
00:15:52,880 --> 00:15:57,177
So that means, it doesn't matter whether
we clear the game or not anymore.

237
00:15:57,260 --> 00:16:01,460
Everyone here is on a time
limit, and once that's up…

238
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:09,560
I want to stay with you forever.

239
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:16,680
I want us to go on real dates,
and to really get married,

240
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:19,240
and for us to grow old together.

241
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:22,657
That's why.

242
00:16:22,740 --> 00:16:23,860
That's why.

243
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:28,717
We don't have a choice.

244
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:30,420
We have to keep fighting.

245
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:53,330
Hey!

246
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:56,330
No way.

247
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:58,032
You guys are coming too?

248
00:16:58,340 --> 00:16:59,497
That's the best you got?

249
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:00,410
No way?

250
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:04,657
Hey, man, I shut my shop down to
come out here and help get this done.

251
00:17:04,740 --> 00:17:08,197
Brother, you're looking at a player who's
about as philanthropic as they come.

252
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:10,297
Then seeing as how
you're so philanthropic,

253
00:17:10,380 --> 00:17:12,337
you're not going to mind if
we take you off the dropless.

254
00:17:12,420 --> 00:17:14,596
